1.44.m:
And he, having ascertained by marks, addressed the destroyer of Tripura.
The Daitya said:
“Desiring to obtain a boon through penance, I went to the Himālaya;

The goddess said:
“By arduous penance, Śaṃkara was indeed attained by me as husband;
yet in secret he has repeatedly called me ‘dark-complexioned one.’
